-- title:
--   Bounded denominators on X_H(M) from A-integral j-values
-- statement:
--   Fix a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, a nonzero natural number $M$ and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Write $F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` for the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the level-$\Gamma_H(M)$ function field `xHFunctionField M H` $\subset \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $x \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is $q^{-1}$ times the power series $E_4^3 \cdot$ `dedekindEtaUnitInv` with integer coefficients cast into $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant $j$. Let $f \in F$ be nonzero and assume that for every place $W$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ — a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and whose ideals are principal, with $W.\mathrm{ord}$ the negative logarithm of the associated adic valuation — such that $W.\mathrm{ord}\, f < 0$ there exists $a \in A$ with $W.\mathrm{ord}\,(x - a) > 0$, the element $a$ being viewed in $F$ through the structure map. Then there is a nonzero $c \in \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every coefficient, indexed by $k \in \mathbb{Z}$, of the Laurent series $c \cdot f$ lies in $A$.
--
--   This is a form of the $q$-expansion principle, or bounded-denominator statement, at level $\Gamma_H(M)$: a function on $X_H(M)$ whose poles all lie over $j$-values that are $A$-integral has, after scaling by a single nonzero constant, an $A$-integral $q$-expansion. It is used in the construction of prolongation data for places of $X_H$, where bases of Riemann–Roch spaces must be normalised so that their expansions have coefficients in a prescribed valuation ring.
-- source:
